      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-87467",
      ":question/problem": "The commodities broker sells $x$ units of a particular commodity at a price per unit $p(x)$, in thousands of dollars, given by\n\n$p(x) = x^{2} - 12x + 21 + \\frac{100}{x}$.\n\nThe broker must sell at least one unit per day and is allowed to sell a maximum of $8$ units per day. How many units should the broker sell to maximize their revenue?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
