      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-87566",
      ":question/problem": "An electronic store sells $x$ mice every day at a price per mouse $p(x)$, in dollars, given by\n$p(x) = x + \\frac{3}{x} + \\frac{54}{x^{2}}$.\n\nIf the store sells between $3$ and $10$ mice per day, how many mice should it sell daily to maximize its revenue?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
